IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`
IMPORT `fraud-dates`
IMPORT `fraud-seat`

-- Fraud Act 2006: CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- One or more cases for each question in fraud-seat.l4, each asked as a person who may be accused
-- would ask it.  Every expected value was decided by reading the section and is written beside the
-- assertion; none was copied from the output.  Arguments are given in the order the question's
-- GIVEN lists them.

§ `Cases for the seat`

-- Short names for the questions, so the assertions below stay on one line each.  They add no law.
`Q fraud` MEANS `On what I have said, am I guilty of fraud under section 1, in any of the three ways in sections 2 to 4`
`Q s2` MEANS `Am I in breach of section 2 (fraud by false representation)`
`Q s3` MEANS `Am I in breach of section 3 (fraud by failing to disclose information)`
`Q s4` MEANS `Am I in breach of section 4 (fraud by abuse of position)`
`Q s6` MEANS `Am I guilty of an offence under section 6 by having this article`
`Q s7` MEANS `Am I guilty of an offence under section 7 by making, adapting, supplying or offering to supply this article`
`Q s9` MEANS `Am I guilty of an offence under section 9 by taking part in this business`
`Q s11` MEANS `Am I guilty of an offence under section 11 by obtaining these services`

§§ `Fraud (sections 1 to 5)`

-- Q fraud arguments: dishonest, gain meant, gain in, loss meant, loss in, about, made to, untrue, misleading, knew,
-- failed to disclose, legal duty, trust position, abused.

-- Section 2 route only: untrue statement to a person, known to be untrue, dishonest, aiming at a gain of money.
#ASSERT `Q fraud` TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Section 3 route only: no statement, a failure to disclose what he had a legal duty to disclose, dishonest, gain of real property.
#ASSERT `Q fraud` TRUE TRUE `real property` FALSE `money` `a fact` `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Section 4 route only: a position of trust, abused, dishonest, aiming at causing a loss in money.
#ASSERT `Q fraud` TRUE FALSE `money` TRUE `money` `a fact` `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Not dishonest on any route (s 2(1)(a), 3(a), 4(1)(b)): no offence.
#ASSERT NOT `Q fraud` FALSE TRUE `money` FALSE `money` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Dishonest, but aiming at a service (s 5(2): not money or other property), on every route: no offence.
#ASSERT NOT `Q fraud` TRUE TRUE `something that is neither money nor property` FALSE `money` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Dishonest, but no aim at all: no offence on any route.
#ASSERT NOT `Q fraud` TRUE FALSE `money` FALSE `money` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Nothing done: no representation, no failure to disclose, no position abused.
#ASSERT NOT `Q fraud` TRUE TRUE `money` TRUE `money` `a fact` `a person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Q s2 arguments: about, made to, untrue, misleading, knew, dishonest, gain meant, gain in, loss meant, loss in.
-- The base case for section 2.
#ASSERT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(3): a representation about the law, or about a state of mind, counts.
#ASSERT `Q s2` `the law` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
#ASSERT `Q s2` `the state of mind of any other person` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(2)(a): misleading and not untrue still counts.
#ASSERT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(2)(a): neither untrue nor misleading: not false.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(2)(b): untrue but he neither knows nor suspects it: not false within s 2(2).
#ASSERT NOT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(5): submitted to a system or device designed to receive communications: made.
#ASSERT `Q s2` `a fact` `a system or device designed to receive, convey or respond to communications` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(5): submitted to nobody: not made.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s2` `a fact` `nobody and nothing: it was not communicated` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(1)(a): not dishonest.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(1)(b)(ii): the aim is a risk of loss in money, not a gain.
#ASSERT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `money` TRUE `money`
-- s 5(2): the aim is a gain in a service, which is neither money nor property.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `something that is neither money nor property` FALSE `money`
-- s 5(2): a gain in a thing in action counts as property.
#ASSERT `Q s2` `a fact` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a thing in action` FALSE `money`
-- s 2(3): something other than fact, law or state of mind is not a representation within the section.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s2` `something other than fact, law or state of mind` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`

-- Q s3 arguments: failed, legal duty, dishonest, gain meant, gain in, loss meant, loss in.
#ASSERT `Q s3` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 3(a): no legal duty to disclose.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s3` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 3: disclosed.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s3` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 3(a): not dishonest.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s3` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 3(b)(ii): the aim is to expose another to a risk of loss in personal property.
#ASSERT `Q s3` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `money` TRUE `personal property`
-- s 3(b): no aim at all.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s3` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `money` FALSE `money`

-- Q s4 arguments: trust position, abused, dishonest, gain meant, gain in, loss meant, loss in.
#ASSERT `Q s4` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 4(1)(a): no position of trust.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s4` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 4(1)(b): did not abuse it.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s4` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 4(1)(b): not dishonest.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s4` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `money` FALSE `money`
-- s 4(1)(c): causing loss to another in real property.
#ASSERT `Q s4` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `money` TRUE `real property`
-- s 5(2): a gain in a favour is not property.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s4` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `something that is neither money nor property` FALSE `money`

§§ `Articles for use in frauds (sections 6 to 8)`

-- Q s6 arguments: what the thing is, in possession, under control, for use in fraud.
#ASSERT `Q s6` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- s 6(1): control suffices.
#ASSERT `Q s6` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- s 8(1): electronic data is an article.
#ASSERT `Q s6` `data held in electronic form` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Q s6` `a program held in electronic form` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- s 6(1): not for use in a fraud.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s6` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 6(1): neither possession nor control.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s6` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- s 6(1): not an article at all.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s6` `none of these` TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- Q s7 arguments: what the thing is, what he did, knew it was designed or adapted for fraud, meant it to be used in a fraud.
#ASSERT `Q s7` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` `makes it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Q s7` `a program held in electronic form` `supplies it` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Q s7` `data held in electronic form` `offers to supply it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Q s7` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` `adapts it` TRUE FALSE
-- s 7(1): neither knowledge nor intention.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s7` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` `makes it` FALSE FALSE
-- s 7(1): none of the four dealings.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s7` `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` `does none of these` TRUE TRUE
-- s 7(1): not an article.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s7` `none of these` `makes it` TRUE TRUE

§§ `Participating in fraudulent business (section 9)`

-- Q s9 arguments: knowingly a party, who carries on the business, intent to defraud creditors, another fraudulent purpose.
#ASSERT `Q s9` TRUE `a person outside the reach of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006, such as a sole trader` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Q s9` TRUE `a person outside the reach of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006, such as a sole trader` FALSE TRUE
-- s 9(2)(a): a company is within the reach of s 993, so s 9 does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s9` TRUE `a company (as defined in section 1(1) of the Companies Act 2006)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Q s9` TRUE `a person to whom section 993 of the Companies Act 2006 applies as if the person were a company` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Q s9` TRUE `a person exempted from the application of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006` TRUE TRUE
-- s 9(1): not knowingly a party.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s9` FALSE `a person outside the reach of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006, such as a sole trader` TRUE TRUE
-- s 9(2)(b): no fraudulent purpose.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s9` TRUE `a person outside the reach of section 993 of the Companies Act 2006, such as a sole trader` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Obtaining services dishonestly (section 11)`

-- Q s11 arguments: obtained, dishonest act, made available on the basis of payment, payment, knew the basis, meant not to pay.
#ASSERT `Q s11` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE TRUE
-- s 11(2)(b): part payment, meaning not to pay the rest.
#ASSERT `Q s11` TRUE TRUE TRUE `payment was made, but not in full` TRUE TRUE
-- s 11(2)(b): paid in full.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s11` TRUE TRUE TRUE `payment was made in full` TRUE TRUE
-- s 11(2)(c): did not mean to withhold payment.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s11` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE
-- s 11(2)(c): did not know the basis.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s11` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` FALSE TRUE
-- s 11(2)(a): a free service: no breach of subsection (2).
#ASSERT NOT `Q s11` TRUE TRUE FALSE `no payment was made` TRUE TRUE
-- s 11(1): not dishonest.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s11` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE TRUE
-- s 11(1): nothing obtained.
#ASSERT NOT `Q s11` FALSE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE TRUE

§§ `What can follow if I am convicted`

-- Longest term on indictment: offence, place.
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `fraud (section 1)` `England` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `possession etc. of articles for use in frauds (section 6)` `Wales` EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `making or supplying articles for use in frauds (section 7)` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `participating in fraudulent business carried on by sole trader etc. (section 9)` `England` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `obtaining services dishonestly (section 11)` `England` EQUALS JUST 5
-- Not covered by the Act: Scotland and anywhere else (s 15(2)); section 10 is blank in this text; conspiracy to defraud is named, not created.
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `fraud (section 1)` `Scotland` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `fraud (section 1)` `anywhere else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `participating in fraudulent business carried on by company etc.: penalty (section 10, blank in this text)` `England` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted on indictment` `conspiracy to defraud (named in section 13(4); this Act creates no such offence)` `England` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Longest term before a magistrates' court: offence, place, date committed.
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `fraud (section 1)` `England` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15) EQUALS JUST `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`
-- Sch 2 para 1: before 2 May 2022, six months.
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `fraud (section 1)` `England` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) EQUALS JUST `six months`
-- The day itself is not "before".
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `fraud (section 1)` `England` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 2) EQUALS JUST `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`
-- ss 1(4), 6(3), 7(3), 9(7), 11(4): Northern Ireland, six months, whatever the date.
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `fraud (section 1)` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15) EQUALS JUST `six months`
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `obtaining services dishonestly (section 11)` `Northern Ireland` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15) EQUALS JUST `six months`
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `possession etc. of articles for use in frauds (section 6)` `Wales` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15) EQUALS JUST `the general limit in a magistrates' court (the Act states no figure)`
#ASSERT `What is the longest prison term I can be given if I am convicted by a magistrates' court` `fraud (section 1)` `Scotland` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 15) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The most fine: offence, place, how convicted.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined if I am convicted` `fraud (section 1)` `England` `summary conviction` EQUALS JUST `the statutory maximum (the Act states no figure)`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined if I am convicted` `fraud (section 1)` `England` `conviction on indictment` EQUALS JUST `no limit is stated`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined if I am convicted` `possession etc. of articles for use in frauds (section 6)` `Northern Ireland` `summary conviction` EQUALS JUST `the statutory maximum (the Act states no figure)`
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined if I am convicted` `fraud (section 1)` `Scotland` `summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Liability of company officers (section 12)`

-- Arguments: a body corporate committed an offence, consent proved, connivance proved, my capacity, in connection with management.
#ASSERT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a director` FALSE
#ASSERT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` TRUE FALSE TRUE `a manager` FALSE
-- s 12(2): no consent or connivance proved.
#ASSERT NOT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` TRUE FALSE FALSE `a director` FALSE
-- s 12(1): not committed by a body corporate.
#ASSERT NOT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` FALSE TRUE TRUE `a director` FALSE
-- s 12(2): none of the listed capacities.
#ASSERT NOT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` TRUE TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE
-- s 12(3): a member of a body managed by its members counts as a director for acts in connection with management.
#ASSERT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `If a company I am an officer of committed an offence under this Act, am I guilty of it too` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members` FALSE

§§ `Evidence (section 13)`

-- Arguments: kind of proceedings, what is required, who may be incriminated, of what kind of offence.
#ASSERT `Am I excused from answering a question, or obeying an order, in proceedings about property because it might incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence under this Act` EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
#ASSERT `Am I excused from answering a question, or obeying an order, in proceedings about property because it might incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner` `proceedings for the execution of a trust` `to comply with an order made` `the person's spouse or civil partner` `conspiracy to defraud` EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
-- The Act says nothing about other proceedings.
#ASSERT `Am I excused from answering a question, or obeying an order, in proceedings about property because it might incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner` `other proceedings` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence under this Act` EQUALS `section 13(1) does not apply`
#ASSERT `Am I excused from answering a question, or obeying an order, in proceedings about property because it might incriminate me or my spouse or civil partner` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence of none of these kinds` EQUALS `section 13(1) does not apply`

-- Arguments: said in answering such a question, the offence in the proceedings where it is used, against whom, married after.
#ASSERT `Can what I said in answering that question, or obeying that order, be used in evidence against me or my spouse or civil partner` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the person who made it` FALSE EQUALS `not admissible in evidence`
#ASSERT `Can what I said in answering that question, or obeying that order, be used in evidence against me or my spouse or civil partner` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the spouse or civil partner of the person who made it` FALSE EQUALS `not admissible in evidence`
-- The exception: they married or became civil partners after the statement was made.
#ASSERT `Can what I said in answering that question, or obeying that order, be used in evidence against me or my spouse or civil partner` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the spouse or civil partner of the person who made it` TRUE EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`
#ASSERT `Can what I said in answering that question, or obeying that order, be used in evidence against me or my spouse or civil partner` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `anyone else` FALSE EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`
#ASSERT `Can what I said in answering that question, or obeying that order, be used in evidence against me or my spouse or civil partner` FALSE `an offence under this Act` `the person who made it` FALSE EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`

§§ `Where and when the Act applies`

#ASSERT `Does the Fraud Act extend to the place where I did it` `England`
#ASSERT `Does the Fraud Act extend to the place where I did it` `Wales`
#ASSERT `Does the Fraud Act extend to the place where I did it` `Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Fraud Act extend to the place where I did it` `Scotland`
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Fraud Act extend to the place where I did it` `anywhere else`

-- Arguments: an order has appointed a day, the day appointed, the day I did it.  The day is made up.
#ASSERT `Was the Fraud Act in force on the day I did it` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15)
#ASSERT `Was the Fraud Act in force on the day I did it` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2008 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Was the Fraud Act in force on the day I did it` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2007 1 14)
-- No order: not in force on any day (the date given is ignored).
#ASSERT NOT `Was the Fraud Act in force on the day I did it` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1)

-- Arguments: first event, last event, the day paragraph 1 of Schedule 1 came into force (made up).
#ASSERT `Can I still be prosecuted for an old deception offence that the Fraud Act abolished` (YearMonthDay 2007 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2007 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) EQUALS `liability is saved by paragraph 3 of Schedule 2`
#ASSERT `Can I still be prosecuted for an old deception offence that the Fraud Act abolished` (YearMonthDay 2007 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2007 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) EQUALS `the offence was abolished before any of its relevant events: no liability under it`
#ASSERT `Can I still be prosecuted for an old deception offence that the Fraud Act abolished` (YearMonthDay 2006 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2007 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2007 1 15) EQUALS `the Act does not say (every relevant event was before commencement, or none is given)`
